From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:01:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Validate room packets and bound relay traffic

The room trusted every packet it received:

- The event loop read data[0] of every packet, also of empty ones.
- Proxy and LDN handlers skipped header fields with IgnoreBytes, which
  does no bounds check, and relayed packets of any size to every member.
- Join, chat, game info and moderation handlers used fields without
  checking that the packet actually contained them.
- Any exception from a handler ended the room thread and the room.

Now:

- Empty packets are dropped before dispatch.
- Chat, game info, kick, ban and unban packets that fail to parse are
  dropped with a warning.
- Proxy and LDN packets must hold their whole header (17 and 11 bytes),
  and are dropped above 1536 bytes. Nintendo's Pia sends at most about
  1472 bytes of UDP payload, plus up to 21 bytes of room header, so real
  game traffic passes; the cap bounds what one packet can make the room
  broadcast to everyone.
- EDEN_ROOM_RELAY_BUDGET_KBPS (default 0 = off) limits how many relay
  bytes per second one member may send. Each relayed packet fans out to
  every other member, so this bounds the egress one member can cause.
  Packets over the budget are dropped for the rest of that second, with
  one warning per second. Too low a value drops real game traffic, which
  is why it is off by default.
- An exception in a handler is logged and the loop continues.

The relayed bytes are not changed: valid packets are forwarded exactly as
before.

Tests: tests/test_room_protocol.py sends empty, truncated, oversized and
malformed packets and checks that they are not relayed and that normal
relay keeps working afterwards.
